-- The default is on a record's field that a helper reads by taking the record
-- apart (CONSIDER ... WHEN Standing g y THEN g). No selector is named anywhere,
-- but the process handles a Standing, and the condition `ok s` is opaque text, so
-- an instance that holds a Standing without the field does not get TRUE.
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Member
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF pay

DECLARE Standing HAS
    `in good standing` IS A BOOLEAN TYPICALLY TRUE
    `years a member`   IS A NUMBER

GIVEN s IS A Standing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ok` s MEANS
  CONSIDER s
  WHEN Standing g y THEN g

GIVEN s IS A Standing
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the duty` s MEANS
    PARTY Member
    MUST pay
    PROVIDED `ok` s
    WITHIN 14
